L000700	
L000701	Gathering all the evidence, we consider it promising to conjecture
L000702	
L000703	\footnote{
L000704	The most ambitious conjecture would be that the 3D $SU(N_f)$ PCM~\eqref{eq:lowT_EFT} is asymptotically safe~\cite{Wilson:1973jj,Weinberg:1976xy} and gives a path-integral description of the 3D $SU(N_f)_{\theta_B}$ field theory, such that (schematically) $g_c^{-2}-g^{-2}\sim\mu$ for a critical coupling $g_c$.
L000705	}
L000706	
L000707	the existence of 3D $SU(N_f)_{\theta_B}$ CFTs, though further tests are
L000708	needed. Should these CFTs exist, it would be natural for QCD to realize
L000709	the conformal-manifold scenario in the chiral limit from $N_f=2$ to the
L000710	lower edge of the conformal window.
L000711	
L000712	
L000713	
L000714	{\bf Outlook.}
L000715	
L000716	
L000717	Recent lattice results~\cite{Cuteri:2021ikv,Dini:2021hug,Nakamura:2022abk,Zhang:2022kzb,Zhang:2024ldl,Zhang:2025vns,Klinger:2025xxb,DAmbrosio:2025ldv,Klinger:2026pbe}
L000718	on the QCD chiral transition motivate our conclusion that only three scenarios
L000719	(Fig.~\ref{fig:allowed_scenarios}) are consistent with a natural
L000720	second-order critical line.  Lattice QCD simulations should distinguish
L000721	them by measuring the leading IR behaviors of $\rho_B$ at
L000722	$\theta_B =0,\pi$ on the critical line, in
L000723	Table~\ref{tab:fingerprints}.
L000724	\begin{table}[ht]
L000725	    \centering
L000726	    \renewcommand{\arraystretch}{1.5}
L000727	    \begin{tabular}{|c|c|c|c|}
L000728	        \hline
L000729	         $\theta_B$ & \textbf{Landau} & \textbf{Landau-DQCP} & \textbf{Conformal-manifold}  \\
L000730	        \hline
L000731	        $0$ & irrelevant & irrelevant & exactly marginal \\ \hline
L000732	        $\pi$ & $\langle\rho_B\rangle\neq0$ & relevant & exactly marginal \\ \hline
L000733	    \end{tabular}
L000734	    \caption{The leading IR behaviors of the operator $\rho_B$ at $\theta_B =0,\pi$ on the critical line.}
L000735	    \label{tab:fingerprints}
L000736	\end{table}
L000737	
L000738	The conformal-manifold scenario is the only option not disfavored for
L000739	$N_f\ge3$ by current evidence. However, it requires the
L000740	$SU(N_f)_{\theta_B}$ universality class, whose existence is an open
L000741	question of independent interest. Demonstrating it will require improved
L000742	conformal bootstrap bounds on 3D CFTs with the
L000743	symmetry~\eqref{eq:3D_IR_symmetry} and further development of the
L000744	$(2+\epsilon)$D expansion. Lattice Monte Carlo simulations of the 3D
L000745	$SU(N_f)$ PCM using L\"uscher's admissibility
L000746	method~\cite{Luscher:1981zq,Schramm:2000cc,Shiozaki:2024yrm,Lopez-Contreras:2025iik}
L000747	(see also Ref.~\cite{Chen:2024ddr}) might be valuable.
L000748	
L000749	While we assume a second-order critical line, a \emph{weakly}
L000750	first-order transition is not excluded by
L000751	Refs.~\cite{Cuteri:2021ikv,Dini:2021hug,Nakamura:2022abk,Zhang:2022kzb,Zhang:2024ldl,Zhang:2025vns,Klinger:2025xxb,DAmbrosio:2025ldv,Klinger:2026pbe}.
L000752	If such transitions are controlled by nearby
L000753	non-unitary complex CFTs~\cite{Gorbenko:2018ncu,Gorbenko:2018dtm}, such
L000754	as the $(2+\epsilon)$D fixed points, much of our discussion would carry
L000755	over.
L000756	
L000757	Finally, we should extend our analysis to real chemical
L000758	potentials. Thermal QCD with real $\mu_B$ violates 3D reflection
L000759	positivity (i.e.~unitarity) but remains ``real'' thanks to anti-unitary
L000760	symmetries related to time reversal. The $SU(N_f)_{\theta_B}$
L000761	conformal manifold might analytically continue to a strip around
L000762	$\theta_B\in\R$. If so, the chiral phase transition could be described
L000763	by non-unitary real CFTs~\cite{Gorbenko:2018ncu,Gorbenko:2018dtm} for
L000764	small real $\mu_B$, and become first-order for larger real $\mu_B$.
L000765	Testing this requires further work.
